From b9c298f4b57ba4c7917f0c7b7666daff8588021f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Agnya <manthram@Pradass-MacBook-Pro.local>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 22:36:47 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Add real onboarding flow: profile setup + travel preferences

New /onboarding page (client/src/pages/onboarding.tsx), two steps:
1. Basic profile (display name, location, bio) -- PATCHes /api/me/profile,
   a small purpose-built form rather than reusing the full ProfileEditor
   (which isn't exported and includes avatar-picker complexity this
   moment doesn't need).
2. Travel preferences -- reuses the existing PreferencesForm component
   as-is (it's self-contained, already handles its own fetch/save/redirect
   to home on success). Both steps have a "skip for now" escape hatch;
   nothing here is a hard gate.

First-time detection (client/src/utils/onboarding.ts): a user is routed
to /onboarding instead of home if their account is under a week old AND
profileCompletePct is under 30 -- both real fields already returned by
/api/auth/me, not new ones.

Wired into all three places a session can start: auth-signin.tsx (the
main Google/Facebook flow), auth-callback.tsx (OAuth redirect landing),
and auth-magic.tsx (magic-link verification). auth-callback and
auth-magic read the user via a ref rather than the value captured when
their effect first ran, since the auth query hasn't necessarily resolved
yet at that point -- reading a stale closure would silently skip
onboarding for every new user. Also removed a redundant, less accurate
onSuccess-callback redirect in auth-signin.tsx that raced against the
already-correct useEffect and would have won.

